chapter Study

session Orphan_Absence = DBLog_Framework_Core +
  description "
    Additive theory on top of the Generalized DBLog contract core:
    the window-discard emission extended with enumerated absence
    entries (per-key absent events for keys read as absent and
    untouched inside the bracket), replayed from an ARBITRARY initial
    sink state. Covers the sink-expanded range record, the connector
    sink-read variant, dense-key enumeration and inventory digests as
    choices of the enumeration. Orphan_Absence_Range_Merge does the
    same for the core's buffered range merge (Flink CDC), with the
    held-back deletes re-emitted at the close, and
    Orphan_Absence_Composition composes a full pass with a later
    bracketed read such as a key-list request. Orphan_Absence_Interleaved
    serves a key-list request while the pass is still running,
    Orphan_Absence_Replay transfers the results to in-order
    at-least-once delivery of each key's events, and
    Orphan_Absence_Tiling proves that a pass's chunk ranges tile the
    key space and are exact for their reads, with a bridge to the
    contract, and Orphan_Absence_Restart states the stream a sink sees
    across one connector restart. Nothing in the archived development is
    modified; this session only imports it.
  "
  options [timeout = 600]
  theories
    Orphan_Absence
    Orphan_Absence_Range_Merge
    Orphan_Absence_Composition
    Orphan_Absence_Interleaved
    Orphan_Absence_Replay
    Orphan_Absence_Tiling
    Orphan_Absence_Restart
